WEBVTT

00:02.002 --> 00:04.045
When Stanley attacks...

00:04.129 --> 00:06.756
Three thousand meters, one second.

00:07.841 --> 00:10.260
...everyone, friend and foe alike,
will turn to stone.

00:11.469 --> 00:14.723
Then, the one who got away
from the beam's range

00:14.806 --> 00:16.599
will lift the petrification
from our allies.

00:16.683 --> 00:18.143
That will seal our victory.

00:18.226 --> 00:20.770
The reviver role,
who will hide far from the main camp,

00:20.854 --> 00:22.856
is insanely important.

00:23.898 --> 00:26.693
You'll be the one splitting off, Suika.

00:27.277 --> 00:30.071
If the job's about hiding,
you can count on me!

00:30.155 --> 00:34.367
That's definitely safer than getting
involved in the battle here, but...

00:35.827 --> 00:38.496
Don't worry. François will join her.

00:38.580 --> 00:40.957
I'll take care of the daily necessities.

00:45.795 --> 00:48.965
- Then, we're hiding close to the river?
- Yes.

00:49.841 --> 00:52.594
We can gather provisions
from time to time,

00:52.677 --> 00:55.430
but we can't survive without water.

00:55.513 --> 01:00.226
Besides, Stanley's crew
is most likely heading upstream by now.

01:00.310 --> 01:03.730
If we keep a close eye on the river,
we might discover something as well.

01:05.690 --> 01:07.984
What's the matter, Miss Suika?

01:10.695 --> 01:12.864
I think I found them.

01:14.532 --> 01:16.076
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA "JUMP COMICS"

02:52.630 --> 02:54.173
- Clear.
- Clear.

02:54.799 --> 02:55.675
Move out.

02:56.676 --> 02:59.637
We'll go ahead of the main force
and scout the surroundings

02:59.721 --> 03:01.514
to secure your route.

03:01.598 --> 03:02.473
Good.

03:05.184 --> 03:07.896
We can just watch for smoke.

03:07.979 --> 03:09.272
Yes.

03:09.355 --> 03:12.358
The Science Club kids' goal
lies here, in Araxá.

03:12.442 --> 03:13.818
That's ore mining.

03:14.485 --> 03:17.363
We'll make sure
to unleash all our firepower.

03:17.447 --> 03:19.032
- Hurry up, hostage!
- Huh...

03:20.950 --> 03:23.536
They've got Ginro and Matsukaze.

03:23.620 --> 03:26.748
This is a wonderful accomplishment,
Miss Suika.

03:26.831 --> 03:30.960
We have to warn everyone else
that Stanley has arrived.

03:31.044 --> 03:34.297
No, the communication device
must be our last resort.

03:34.380 --> 03:36.758
If we broadcast now, they'll trace us.

03:37.508 --> 03:41.512
We are key players in our strategy.
We can't afford to take any risks.

03:43.556 --> 03:46.017
<i>Even the monsters in the Amazon</i>

03:46.100 --> 03:49.312
<i>keep their distance
to avoid the ultimate creature.</i>

03:52.315 --> 03:54.734
Let's return briefly to let everyone know.

04:06.454 --> 04:07.622
This is terrible!

04:07.705 --> 04:11.084
It looks like something
has bitten one of the enemies.

04:12.252 --> 04:14.295
This is the final emergency item

04:14.379 --> 04:16.673
for dealing with poison and the like.

04:17.298 --> 04:21.052
It's a patch stained
with the nitroglycerin used in dynamite.

04:21.135 --> 04:24.430
Just by applying it to the body,
it dilates the coronary arteries

04:24.514 --> 04:27.016
and jolts the heart back to life.

04:27.976 --> 04:32.313
But we are key players in this battle.
If they discover us...

04:53.209 --> 04:57.588
Stanley won't hesitate
to slaughter all of you

04:57.672 --> 05:01.092
to make sure I'm rescued as the General.

05:01.759 --> 05:06.556
It's not an ethical issue.
It's his job as a soldier.

05:06.639 --> 05:09.392
Yes, you're right.

05:09.475 --> 05:13.438
But all you do is spout pretty words.

05:13.521 --> 05:15.898
Oh, that's your weak point.

05:17.817 --> 05:20.695
A remarkably fragile cleavage surface!

05:25.366 --> 05:27.493
Why...? I'm one...

05:27.577 --> 05:29.203
of your greatest enemies...

05:29.287 --> 05:31.205
It's okay.

05:33.458 --> 05:34.417
Thank you...

05:34.500 --> 05:36.252
- Freeze!
- Freeze!

05:42.133 --> 05:43.301
- Freeze!
- Freeze!

05:43.885 --> 05:46.220
Freeze? What does 'freeze' mean?

05:46.304 --> 05:48.139
I'm afraid I only remember vaguely,

05:48.222 --> 05:51.350
but doesn't it mean 'to freeze'?

05:52.018 --> 05:53.978
<i>I don't understand them at all,</i>

05:54.062 --> 05:57.774
<i>but they definitely can't catch us!</i>

05:57.857 --> 05:59.233
Get her!

05:59.317 --> 06:02.487
She'll report our presence and position
to their base!

06:02.570 --> 06:04.489
<i>This is serious.</i>

06:04.572 --> 06:06.824
<i>There's no way Suika,
who never knew the 21st century,</i>

06:06.908 --> 06:10.203
<i>would understand
that 'freeze' means 'don't move'.</i>

06:13.915 --> 06:18.461
<i>My only weapon is this one kitchen knife.</i>

06:18.544 --> 06:20.546
<i>And I have no fighting ability whatsoever.</i>

06:21.255 --> 06:24.050
<i>If I recklessly rush out
armed with only a knife,</i>

06:24.717 --> 06:27.303
<i>I'll just get myself and Suika
gunned down.</i>

06:27.386 --> 06:28.346
<i>So...</i>

06:28.429 --> 06:29.722
Don't let her get away!

06:29.806 --> 06:33.226
<i>I'm counting on you,
Mr. Matsukaze and Mr. Ginro!</i>

06:35.520 --> 06:38.397
<i>Back then, I put my life on the line</i>

06:38.940 --> 06:40.983
<i>to perfect my throwing skills!</i>

06:42.151 --> 06:43.069
Fire!

06:44.529 --> 06:48.157
<i>With my hands tied behind my back,
it's impossible to cut myself free.</i>

06:48.908 --> 06:50.118
<i>So...</i>

06:56.249 --> 06:58.167
I'm counting on you, Master Ginro!

06:58.251 --> 07:00.670
- The rope...
- Get him!

07:00.753 --> 07:04.173
<i>Matsukaze, you idiot!
There's nothing I can do against guns!</i>

07:04.799 --> 07:07.301
<i>But... At this close range...</i>

07:10.138 --> 07:13.516
<i>No, no, no! I'll be killed if I move!</i>

07:13.599 --> 07:15.935
<i>Why do I have to be killed?</i>

07:16.018 --> 07:18.688
<i>It's all Matsukaze's fault!
Just stay put and behave!</i>

07:23.568 --> 07:24.485
<i>The Chief...</i>

07:25.153 --> 07:27.655
<i>...remained strong until the very end.</i>

07:37.915 --> 07:40.334
I won't let you!

07:40.418 --> 07:43.963
I won't let you shoot Suika!

07:51.596 --> 07:52.597
That's right...

07:52.680 --> 07:56.309
I had forgotten, but I was actually
the village gatekeeper!

07:56.392 --> 07:58.186
I was pretty strong!

07:58.269 --> 08:00.563
I went through some amazing training!

08:02.690 --> 08:03.691
Huh?

08:08.863 --> 08:11.240
Argh!

08:11.324 --> 08:13.242
It hurts!

08:14.160 --> 08:16.412
<i>For someone so skilled like Stanley...</i>

08:17.038 --> 08:20.708
<i>Why didn't he shoot Mr. Ginro just now?</i>

08:20.791 --> 08:23.169
<i>He could have shot him
before he went on a rampage.</i>

08:24.295 --> 08:26.422
<i>Only one reason comes to mind.</i>

08:26.506 --> 08:28.341
<i>It wasn't that he chose not to fire,</i>

08:28.424 --> 08:32.178
<i>but that he wouldn't fire until Mr. Ginro,
being a captive, initiated an attack.</i>

08:32.762 --> 08:35.515
<i>Besides, there's no sign
that Mr. Ginro or Mr. Matsukaze</i>

08:35.598 --> 08:38.267
<i>were hurt during their captivity.</i>

08:39.018 --> 08:43.356
<i>They've been treated as prisoners of war
and kept under certain rules.</i>

08:44.315 --> 08:47.610
<i>These men are not murderers, but soldiers!</i>

08:48.277 --> 08:49.529
<i>Which means...</i>

08:52.073 --> 08:55.743
We are civilians! We are civilians!

08:57.703 --> 09:00.581
She is Suika, a civilian doctor.

09:01.791 --> 09:04.085
<i>Fulfilling her duties as a doctor,</i>

09:04.168 --> 09:07.088
<i>she administered treatment
for a poisonous spider bite.</i>

09:07.171 --> 09:12.343
We decided to part ways with Senku's crew
for our own safety.

09:12.426 --> 09:16.305
You're welcome to check our belongings
if you wish.

09:17.139 --> 09:19.809
<i>François's actually not lying...</i>

09:20.393 --> 09:23.187
We don't belong to any army.

09:23.271 --> 09:26.607
We mean no harm and serve everyone.

09:26.691 --> 09:28.734
Are you still going to shoot us?

09:31.320 --> 09:33.698
No, we're not.

09:33.781 --> 09:35.950
As long as you're telling the truth.

09:36.033 --> 09:37.952
Gotcha!

09:46.419 --> 09:49.630
We're in big trouble, and it's my fault.

09:49.714 --> 09:53.843
And we have no way to tell everyone
that Stanley is here.

09:53.926 --> 09:56.679
Not necessarily, Miss Suika.

09:56.762 --> 09:59.056
This might be a good thing, after all.

10:00.975 --> 10:03.561
What's wrong, Leonard?

10:03.644 --> 10:06.355
That butler, François.

10:06.439 --> 10:09.483
He used the radio
right before we caught him.

10:09.567 --> 10:12.320
Yes. If you're interested,

10:12.403 --> 10:15.364
take a look at the contents
of the Morse code.

10:15.448 --> 10:17.074
It said, "We'll split into two groups."

10:17.158 --> 10:20.995
I broadcast through the US mainland
just to be safe.

10:32.757 --> 10:35.259
Did something happen
to Suika and François?

10:35.343 --> 10:38.846
They made contact with Stanley.

10:40.389 --> 10:42.558
So you risked exposing us to the enemy

10:42.642 --> 10:44.727
by sending this signal.

10:45.645 --> 10:49.565
It's the exact opposite.
François just let us know their position.

10:49.649 --> 10:52.902
Sure, it's easy! All I have to do

10:52.985 --> 10:56.822
is track the time since François left
toward the signal.

10:56.906 --> 11:00.409
Yes, we discovered them first.

11:00.993 --> 11:02.036
I can see it...

11:03.079 --> 11:05.331
The place where Stanley is...

11:05.414 --> 11:08.709
Our final battle against Stanley...

11:10.419 --> 11:13.714
<i>The most important information
is the enemy's location,</i>

11:13.798 --> 11:17.009
<i>and we got that first!</i>

11:17.093 --> 11:19.136
Wait, wait!

11:19.220 --> 11:23.015
There's one thing we need to watch out for
the most right now!

11:23.099 --> 11:25.142
Suika and François have been caught.

11:25.226 --> 11:27.061
We even know where the enemy is.

11:27.144 --> 11:30.689
Put those together, and of course
some hero's going to rush in headfirst!

11:30.773 --> 11:34.193
We have to hold her down...
Wait, where is she?

11:36.987 --> 11:40.449
Oh no, we're too late!

11:41.617 --> 11:44.787
It's dangerous, but it could be
our best bet now, don't you think?

11:44.870 --> 11:48.624
Yes, our conditions for victory
are simple.

11:48.707 --> 11:52.670
We have to get the petrification devices
working before the enemy arrives.

11:52.753 --> 11:55.339
We have no choice but to hold Stanley off

11:55.423 --> 11:58.175
with a preemptive guerrilla battle.

12:04.181 --> 12:07.643
<i>Stanley and his group are
both amazing and terrifying.</i>

12:07.726 --> 12:11.730
<i>They can track our footprints,
even when they're barely visible.</i>

12:11.814 --> 12:13.399
<i>At this rate,</i>

12:13.482 --> 12:16.485
<i>they'll discover
where the others are hiding!</i>

12:19.363 --> 12:20.364
<i>That's it.</i>

12:20.990 --> 12:24.034
<i>We know the enemy's current position
and their route,</i>

12:24.618 --> 12:26.620
<i>so with my eyesight,</i>

12:26.704 --> 12:28.914
<i>spotting them
would normally be child's play.</i>

12:28.998 --> 12:29.874
<i>But...</i>

12:30.541 --> 12:34.211
<i>The lead soldier is alert
for ropes and wire traps.</i>

12:34.295 --> 12:37.173
<i>The leader behind him keeps watch
forward and above.</i>

12:37.840 --> 12:39.884
<i>The radio operator scans left and right.</i>

12:40.551 --> 12:42.636
<i>The rearguard watches their back.</i>

12:43.304 --> 12:45.347
<i>Every member advances in perfect order,</i>

12:45.431 --> 12:47.683
<i>maintaining equal spacing.</i>

12:48.851 --> 12:50.478
<i>Not an opening in their formation.</i>

12:52.563 --> 12:55.983
Yes, they're professional soldiers
from the 21st century.

12:56.066 --> 12:58.486
Tsukasa! Hyoga!

12:58.569 --> 13:03.199
The moment you ran out, I thought
your brain had completely melted.

13:03.282 --> 13:05.784
But it's impressive
that you didn't simply rush in

13:05.868 --> 13:09.788
but also assessed the enemy's strength
right before your eyes.

13:10.414 --> 13:13.542
They've trained and prepared
for every possible situation.

13:14.335 --> 13:16.462
There's no way we could win
in a fair fight.

13:17.254 --> 13:19.548
We need to be prepared as well.

13:27.932 --> 13:29.183
That's...

13:30.017 --> 13:32.603
<i>It's one of the records that Chrome made</i>

13:32.686 --> 13:34.855
<i>as a manual, remote-controlled trap.</i>

13:41.946 --> 13:44.657
I think it sounds too weak
to be a gunshot.

13:44.740 --> 13:47.201
Why? It's an actual gunshot.

13:48.118 --> 13:51.121
The real thing
is not always the best option.

13:51.205 --> 13:53.666
For example, in movie sound effects,

13:53.749 --> 13:58.254
flowing sand can be far more effective
than actual ocean waves.

13:58.337 --> 13:59.421
Yes.

13:59.505 --> 14:02.466
How about trying a banging sound
with a plastic container?

14:04.093 --> 14:05.177
It could work!

14:06.178 --> 14:08.389
We'll record the sound of the plastic once

14:08.472 --> 14:10.766
and then play it back at a slower speed.

14:13.018 --> 14:14.645
It sounds good!

14:14.728 --> 14:18.566
Our sonar man Ukyo
has the hearing of a sound director!

14:18.649 --> 14:21.527
Let's layer the sound several times.

14:25.906 --> 14:27.491
- Yikes!
- It's an ambush!

14:27.575 --> 14:31.036
Someone's shooting at us!
We're allies here!

14:35.207 --> 14:37.167
Another team is coming around,

14:37.251 --> 14:39.336
leaving the front line to take the shots.

14:39.420 --> 14:40.796
Did they notice...?

14:40.880 --> 14:43.424
No, they're professionals.

14:43.507 --> 14:47.344
They'd instantly realize
the gunshots are fake, right?

14:47.928 --> 14:51.265
<i>We shouldn't let our guards down
and think we're safe.</i>

14:51.891 --> 14:56.896
<i>They'll counter the ambush
following established procedures.</i>

14:56.979 --> 15:00.482
<i>The designated members
will fire immediately to draw attention,</i>

15:00.566 --> 15:04.361
<i>while the rest will circle around
slowly and engage the enemy.</i>

15:04.445 --> 15:08.198
Then we should use this opportunity
to get Suika and the others back.

15:08.282 --> 15:11.327
That'd be hard. Stanley is next to them.

15:12.077 --> 15:14.496
If there's a melee, the hostages will die.

15:16.290 --> 15:20.085
Let's destroy
their communications instead.

15:20.878 --> 15:23.839
This might be our chance,
in the middle of the fight.

15:23.923 --> 15:26.258
It's a one-in-a-million opportunity.

15:26.342 --> 15:29.386
I see. I too have learned

15:29.470 --> 15:32.306
that communications
are crucial in modern warfare.

15:32.389 --> 15:33.432
No.

15:33.515 --> 15:37.519
In fact, if we monopolize
the communications network,

15:37.603 --> 15:40.648
the battle is won right then and there.

15:40.731 --> 15:42.524
What do you mean?

15:42.608 --> 15:44.151
Just think about it.

15:44.860 --> 15:47.988
<i>We could just
hold a blade to Xeno's throat</i>

15:48.072 --> 15:50.574
<i>and demand Stanley's surrender.</i>

15:51.450 --> 15:56.038
Why do you think we haven't tried
that easy way out yet?

15:56.789 --> 16:00.584
That's because Nikki
and dozens more of our friends

16:00.668 --> 16:02.962
were left behind
as hostages in enemy territory.

16:04.088 --> 16:06.507
There's a balance in
how the hostages are held.

16:06.590 --> 16:08.008
Yes.

16:08.092 --> 16:10.761
If we hurt Xeno,

16:10.844 --> 16:13.639
they'd quickly
contact Corn City in the north,

16:13.722 --> 16:15.265
putting everyone in danger...

16:16.850 --> 16:20.354
<i>Exactly. If they can't
establish communications,</i>

16:20.437 --> 16:23.232
<i>the hostages they hold become meaningless.</i>

16:24.316 --> 16:30.990
Then, if we were to remove Xeno's fingers,
hands, and feet one by one,

16:31.073 --> 16:34.076
we could force Stanley to surrender.

16:34.159 --> 16:36.578
We are not doing that!

16:36.662 --> 16:40.624
Besides, speaking of hostages,
they now have Suika and three others too!

16:40.708 --> 16:43.877
The lives of everyone are at stake.

16:43.961 --> 16:46.505
If our victory depended on
abandoning just four people,

16:46.588 --> 16:49.675
the choice would be obvious.

16:50.467 --> 16:53.387
Did you really think
we'd allow such a plan?

16:54.471 --> 16:59.226
Regardless of whether we carry it out,
as long as it remains an option...

17:00.269 --> 17:02.146
<i>From Stanley's point of view,</i>

17:02.229 --> 17:06.817
<i>if their communications are destroyed,
they'll need to repair them immediately.</i>

17:07.568 --> 17:09.737
<i>It will cost them a lot of time.</i>

17:09.820 --> 17:10.946
Yes.

17:11.613 --> 17:14.658
If that's the only goal, I'm all for it.

17:18.704 --> 17:20.164
What's wrong, Maya?

17:22.750 --> 17:24.543
Don't you know...

17:24.626 --> 17:27.337
the instincts of the US women's
fighting champion?

17:30.049 --> 17:32.092
I found you!

17:32.176 --> 17:33.677
Huh?

17:36.513 --> 17:40.684
Since we are surrounded by enemy guns,
escape is impossible.

17:41.477 --> 17:44.897
Well, our deaths are certain, but...

17:45.647 --> 17:46.899
Yes.

17:46.982 --> 17:50.360
We're not just
going to stand still and get shot.

17:51.945 --> 17:56.200
I never thought the three of us
would end up fighting together as a trio.

17:57.826 --> 17:59.119
<i>Even if we die here,</i>

17:59.953 --> 18:02.539
<i>we have to make sure
their communications are destroyed!</i>

18:03.123 --> 18:06.460
<i>We're fighting for Team Senku's victory!</i>

18:21.391 --> 18:22.851
<i>My back is burning...</i>

18:24.394 --> 18:27.856
<i>If you expose your back even
for an instant, your life will be taken.</i>

18:27.940 --> 18:32.111
<i>The back you show in battle
is freezing to the bone.</i>

18:34.696 --> 18:36.698
<i>But in this final battle,</i>

18:38.283 --> 18:39.952
<i>for the first time, I feel so...</i>

19:07.396 --> 19:09.106
- Tsukasa!
- Go!

19:12.234 --> 19:13.569
That's Tsukasa!

19:13.652 --> 19:14.570
Who?

19:14.653 --> 19:16.905
The strongest high schooler
among primates,

19:16.989 --> 19:19.658
a martial arts champion from Japan!

19:19.741 --> 19:21.618
Huh?

19:21.702 --> 19:24.246
Then, I'll kill him with all my power!

19:57.404 --> 19:59.114
I'm impressed.

19:59.198 --> 20:02.743
No opponent has ever given me
this much trouble before.

20:21.345 --> 20:24.556
He beat Maya! He's a monster...

20:28.060 --> 20:30.771
No matter how strong you are,

20:30.854 --> 20:33.565
you can't stand against weapons
and bullets made with science!

20:36.693 --> 20:40.864
You have no idea how the old world,
controlled by vested interests,

20:40.948 --> 20:45.577
had been completely corrupted
by scientific weapons.

20:46.328 --> 20:48.080
It needed to be stopped.

20:54.002 --> 20:55.337
Tsukasa!

21:04.596 --> 21:09.101
Kohaku! Why are you staring at me?

21:09.184 --> 21:11.395
You've got a job to do!

21:15.357 --> 21:17.276
You don't say?

21:18.443 --> 21:20.362
Yes...

21:20.445 --> 21:24.241
You're doing the right thing...

21:33.542 --> 21:35.961
So, that was your goal...

21:37.337 --> 21:38.505
Yes...

21:39.423 --> 21:40.632
There you go.

22:23.884 --> 22:25.510
You did it...

22:27.095 --> 22:28.180
Yes.

22:28.263 --> 22:30.807
As expected of you two...

22:35.729 --> 22:39.024
<i>Hyoga... is dead...</i>

22:41.735 --> 22:45.781
<i>Kohaku and I... won't last much longer.</i>

22:47.741 --> 22:51.787
<i>Once Senku and his team complete Medusa...</i>

22:53.371 --> 22:55.665
<i>I wonder if its restorative effects...</i>

22:55.749 --> 22:58.210
<i>could even bring the dead back.</i>

23:00.045 --> 23:04.132
<i>Mirai and I,
who had been in suspended animation,</i>

23:04.216 --> 23:05.759
<i>were awakened from our cold sleep...</i>

23:06.635 --> 23:09.721
<i>The only issue is
preserving the cell tissue...</i>

23:10.931 --> 23:12.516
<i>So...</i>

23:18.772 --> 23:21.233
<i>Before I even realized it...</i>

23:22.442 --> 23:26.154
<i>I had entrusted my entire fate
to Senku and his team's science.</i>

